---
import CaseStudy from '../layouts/CaseStudy.astro';

const facts = [
  { k: 'City', v: 'Freiburg' },
  { k: 'Built', v: '1998–2010s' },
  { k: 'Scale', v: 'A district, ~5,000 residents' },
  { k: 'Transit', v: 'Tram in the street' },
  { k: 'Parking', v: 'Pushed to the edge' },
  { k: 'Method', v: 'Many Baugruppen' },
];

const gallery = [
  {
    placeholder: 'Green spine — photo needed',
    cap: 'The green spine between the blocks',
    src: 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Gr%C3%BCnspange%20mit%20Backhaus%20in%20Freiburg-Vauban.jpg?width=1400',
    credit: 'via Wikimedia Commons',
    creditHref: 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gr%C3%BCnspange_mit_Backhaus_in_Freiburg-Vauban.jpg',
  },
  {
    placeholder: 'Street with tram — photo needed',
    cap: "The tram street: the district's largest shared room",
    src: 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Vauban%20Gr%C3%BCnspange%201.jpg?width=1400',
    credit: 'via Wikimedia Commons',
    creditHref: 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vauban_Gr%C3%BCnspange_1.jpg',
  },
  {
    placeholder: 'Baugruppe facades — photo needed',
    cap: 'Many small buildings, many small clients — a car-free Quartiersstrasse',
    src: 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Beispiel%20Quartiersstra%C3%9Fe%20Vauban.jpg?width=1400',
    credit: 'Dr. med. Mabuse · CC BY-SA 3.0',
    creditHref: 'https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Beispiel_Quartiersstra%C3%9Fe_Vauban.jpg',
  },
];
---

<CaseStudy
  title="Vauban"
  subtitle="What a whole street of these buildings feels like."
  heroSrc="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Freiburg%20-%20Vauban.jpg?width=1400"
  heroPlaceholder="Vauban hero"
  heroCredit="via Wikimedia Commons"
  heroCreditHref="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Freiburg_-_Vauban.jpg"
  facts={facts}
  gallery={gallery}
  prev={{ href: '/swans-market/', label: "Swan's Market" }}
  next={{ href: '/hunziker-areal/', label: 'Hunziker Areal' }}
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-[760px] px-6 pt-16 sm:px-12">
    <p class="text-[21px] leading-[1.62]">
      Vauban is not one building — it is what happens when a city lets dozens of building groups
      fill a district with mid-rise blocks: tram down the main street, shops at the ground floors,
      children owning the pavement, cars parked in garages at the edge. A former barracks site
      became the standing proof that the type, repeated, makes a neighborhood and not a project.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-6 text-[21px] leading-[1.62]">
      What to steal: the parceling. Freiburg sold small lots to many Baugruppen instead of large
      lots to few developers — variety, affordability, and speed came from the plural, not from any
      single design.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="lessons">
    <li>Sell small parcels to many groups: variety and affordability come from the plural.</li>
    <li>Parking at the district edge is what gives every block its courtyard back.</li>
    <li>
      The tram is the spine — Berkeley's corridors already have the transit; they lack the street
      walls.
    </li>
    <li>One building first; Vauban is what the tenth one adds up to.</li>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="sources">
    Sources: City of Freiburg and Forum Vauban publications. Resident figure approximate.
  </Fragment>
</CaseStudy>
